Description: Expose Rust FollowWith and FullyQualifiedName traits.
    This supplies compile-time type identity information necessary for
    reflection-based message dispatch and routing tables inside
    real-time Rust environments.
    Implemented by declaring FollowWith in
    rust/flatbuffers/src/follow.rs and FullyQualifiedName in
    rust/flatbuffers/src/primitives.rs, and modifying the Rust
    generator in src/idl_gen_rust.cpp to write implementations of
    FullyQualifiedName (returning the absolute package path, e.g.,
    "MyGame.Monster") for generated structs and tables when the
    --gen-name-strings flag is active, along with FollowWith trait
    mapping.


diff --git a/rust/flatbuffers/src/follow.rs b/rust/flatbuffers/src/follow.rs
index 7488487..6adcd4f 100644
--- a/rust/flatbuffers/src/follow.rs
+++ b/rust/flatbuffers/src/follow.rs
@@ -61,3 +61,7 @@ impl<'a, T: Follow<'a>> Follow<'a> for FollowStart<T> {
         T::follow(buf, loc)
     }
 }
+
+pub trait FollowWith<'a> {
+    type Inner: Follow<'a>;
+}
